**Reverse D606’s postponement reading provisionally, and check the fiscal-year note’s consumers at $0.** The full-rung audit is a reason to change our earlier position: for a dated shipment question, a formal decision that it will not happen by that date can be read as a decision against the event the Yes rung asks about. Preserve the alternative and the card’s tradeoff in the record; do not describe the boundary as settled by Alex. [Audit](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/unlisted-parts/fresh-a2/postponement/AUDIT-RESULT.md), [D409](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:4502).

Two qualifications matter before closing the route:

- **An announcement is not necessarily a decision.** “It will not happen by the date” can be a forecast of delay rather than the company deciding against the dated event. Some dissenting reader reasons make that distinction; it is too strong to say they all ignored the date. Keep a forecast-versus-decision guard in any future reading. [Reader reasons](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/unlisted-parts/fresh-a2/postponement/audit-class.txt).
- **Reconcile the audit’s matter counts.** Its summary says 34 distinct answers over 7 matters and 33 company answers, while the displayed matter rows add to 35 and the six company rows to 34. The raw class output labels 16 groups before the report combines them. This may be an overlap or grouping issue, but the report should show it before the totals are used. [Audit table](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/unlisted-parts/fresh-a2/postponement/AUDIT-RESULT.md), [class output](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/unlisted-parts/fresh-a2/postponement/audit-class.txt).

Subject to those corrections, I agree to **close the proposed postponement repair route**: the audit has not established a missing general instruction. Keep Taiwan’s ruling as a recorded failure under the present reading, without claiming that one send establishes a recurring class. Keep the Kyber window mismatch as a lead on one matter.

The fiscal-note check is a reasonable next step, provided it asks **what a change could affect**, rather than assuming a gate improvement. The note is shared: the ladder payload calls it, and production extraction also puts it in its request. Do not edit the shared function. [Ladder payload](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/stage_a/stage_a.py:141), [extraction request](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/extraction.py:377).

At $0, trace the note’s callers and the ladder’s full request, validation and view-writing path. In particular, determine whether removing the clause could affect the model’s choice of year, basis, refusal or rung—not just the date code ultimately writes. The **128** stored obligation failures name the annual filing, but the D-only diagnostic did not reproduce their split and did not prove the note caused it. [Diagnostic](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/unlisted-parts/fresh-a2/d-diagnostic/RESULT.md).

A result that advances the path is a general, sourced request contradiction with a product-visible or gate-relevant effect and a bounded comparison against the frozen step. Close it as a cleanup-only or unproven-cause lead if the check cannot show that; no new version or paid send follows from the contradiction alone.

CONSENSUS: provisionally reverse the postponement reading, correct the audit’s counts and qualifications, close that repair route, and audit the shared fiscal-year note at $0.
